THIRD-PARTY CONTENT
-------------------

This project incorporates the following public-domain material. Neither is
covered by the copyright above, and each is used on its own terms.

ENABLE word list (data/enable1.txt)
  Enhanced North American Benchmark Lexicon, by Alan Beale and Mendel Cooper.
  Released into the public domain. Filtered before use to remove slurs and
  crude terms; see scripts/lib/blocklist.mjs.

Webster's Unabridged Dictionary, 1913 (data/webster.json)
  Public domain in the United States by virtue of its 1913 publication date.
  Used to derive puzzle clues. Entries whose wording reflects the prejudices
  of their era are excluded at build time; see scripts/lib/blocklist.mjs
  (`containsSlur`) and scripts/lib/defs.mjs.

  PROVENANCE NOTE: the JSON transcription in data/webster.json was obtained
  from a repository that also carries a GPLv2 grant covering its own tooling
  and example outputs. The underlying 1913 text is unambiguously US public
  domain, and a mechanical transcription of a public-domain text attracts no
  new copyright — but the cleanest resolution is to re-derive this file
  directly from the Project Gutenberg edition, stripping the Gutenberg header
  per their terms. That is tracked and not yet done. Until it is, treat the
  transcription's provenance as unresolved rather than settled.

No sampled audio, webfonts or third-party icons are used. Sound is synthesised
at runtime with the Web Audio API; icons are generated by scripts/build-icons.py.
